# CA Private Key for CMS Demo
#
# WARNING: Private keys should NEVER be committed to version control!
#
# This file is a placeholder for the CA private key needed by the CMS demos.
# To run the demos, you need to generate your own private key.
#
# Generate a new CA private key using:
#   openssl genpkey -algorithm RSA -out cakey.pem -pkcs8 -aes256
#
# Or for demo purposes without password protection (INSECURE):
#   openssl genpkey -algorithm RSA -out cakey.pem
#
# Make sure this file matches the public key in cacert.pem for the demos
# to work correctly.
#
# SECURITY NOTE: Keep private keys secure and never share them!
